{
  "_comment": "Shared normalisation rules. Read by tools/update_data.py and by the curator panel in index.html. Edit here only. occasionRules: first rule that matches the PARTICULAR OCCASION text wins (case-insensitive regular expressions); empty, 'Unknown', 'No', 'None' or 'N/A' gives 'Not recorded', no match gives 'Other'. groupAliases, ideologyRules and motiveRules (perpetrator fields): first rule that matches wins (case-insensitive regular expressions); an empty or 'Unknown' value gives 'Not recorded'. No individual names are ever imported. weaponRules: each label lists the patterns that signal it; an incident that matches several labels is 'Multiple types'; the 'generic' explosive label is dropped when a more specific explosive label also matches. Categories only; no technical detail is held. groupTypeRules (perpetrator type): applied to the group name as recorded, first match wins; with no group recorded the type comes from the number of attackers. The type describes the kind of group, never an individual.",
